***********************************Interpretation for some parameters***********************************
#######################
input parameters
    9000     0   8000   ngrid_r0 lmin lmax
         ngrid_r0(ngrid_r in subroutine param_input) is the number of grids in the whole earth. The grids are equal-spacing. 
         To large extents, the accuracy of seismograms depend on this parameter. 

#######################
depth_cutoff - The depth used to determine the cut-off l. The code now can not deal with the target depth equal to the source depth.

#######################
ngrid_r in almost all the subroutines, except param_input, is the final number of grids. We may add zero, one or two nodes when 
         implement a source. There are three possible situations as following (line 229 in param.f) when impement source
         (1) source is located between two nodes. Add one node with grid_r(itmp) = source_r. 
              (a) If the two nodes are the top nodes of this zone and this zone is solid media. Add one more node with 
                  r= ( grid_r(itmp) + source_r ) / 2.d0
              (b) Do nothing if not top node
         (2) source is exactly on the top node of a zone and the zone is solid media. Move the the source a little 
             bit deeper and add two nodes.
         (3) do nothing for other situations. For example, the source is located exactly on one node beneath the top node. 

########################
The maximum number of radial nodes are fixed and they are equal spacing, but after every 100 degree-l iterations, it checks
    'check_amp_significance' to update the cut-off radius and determine whether to finish the computation or not.

